# Tabs in the source and in help text are shown as four spaces.
mode: syntax
---- query
'orders.csv'
|	where	amount > 1	AND	amount < 5
---- expected
PROGRAM@0..47
  PIPELINE@0..46
    LITERAL@0..12
      STRING@0..12 "'orders.csv'"
    WHITESPACE@12..13 "\n"
    PIPE@13..14 "|"
    WHITESPACE@14..15 "\t"
    WHERE_OP@15..46
      IDENT@15..20 "where"
      WHITESPACE@20..21 "\t"
      BIN_EXPR@21..46
        BIN_EXPR@21..31
          NAME_REF@21..27
            IDENT@21..27 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@27..28 " "
          GT@28..29 ">"
          WHITESPACE@29..30 " "
          LITERAL@30..31
            LONG@30..31 "1"
        WHITESPACE@31..32 "\t"
        IDENT@32..35 "AND"
        WHITESPACE@35..36 "\t"
        BIN_EXPR@36..46
          NAME_REF@36..42
            IDENT@36..42 "amount"
          WHITESPACE@42..43 " "
          LT@43..44 "<"
          WHITESPACE@44..45 " "
          LITERAL@45..46
            LONG@45..46 "5"
  WHITESPACE@46..47 "\n"

error[DS0105]: SQL keyword `AND` in capitals
  --> query:2:20
  |
2 | |    where    amount > 1    AND    amount < 5
  |                             ^^^ this is SQL
  |
  = help: write `and` in lowercase: `amount > 1    and    amount < 5`

with the machine-applicable fixes applied:
    'orders.csv'
    |	where	amount > 1	and	amount < 5
which parses without errors
